  "sourceFileCount": 83,
  "notes": "Bridge 1.0.8 candidate source, including the grouped review-repair fixes: external passes move to awaiting-recheck on any new stage, contradictory pass/check receipts are refused before writes, new actionable reviews start a fresh bounded automation cycle, declared-scope logs are excluded from source-progress fingerprints, review IDs map to portable hashed receipt filenames, reviewedSource is preflighted/bounded and streamed rather than whole-file read, receipt idempotency binds the raw body before scrubbing, maintenance guard ASSETS now cover dist/src/history.js, and newly recorded pass/blocked/non-actionable receipts refresh delivery review metadata plus the mutable checkpoint without live-source recapture or sealed-stage rewrites. Adds bounded same-live-session continuation after actual provider output exhaustion (autoContinue with legacy omission disabled and complete-preset defaults), the structured caller-reported external acceptance receipt dsh_submit_review with durable/idempotent receipts and one same-session repair for actionable failure, and separate automation metrics with per-stage cause/elapsed evidence in task/result, checkpoints, delivery/export and bounded history. Preserves 1.0.7 persistence health, deliverySource complete/patch import, bounded events and progress, 1.0.6 checkpoint recovery, 1.0.5 read-only history/export, old tool schemas and legacy delivery Markdown rendering. Version identity is 1.0.8 in package.json, package-lock.json, BRIDGE_VERSION and the MCP capability surface. SDK 0.2.1-rc.2 runtime package baseline entries remain byte-identical; only the candidate-local bridge dist asset hashes were recaptured, and guard.mjs changed only by additive ASSETS coverage. Full scripted suite 293/293 across 28 suites, zero failures/skips/todos. Ubuntu-DSH is the execution target; native Windows execution and native SDK conversation resume are deferred, and the scripted suite makes no real-model or token/time-saving claim. This manifest excludes only SOURCE-HASHES.sha256, docs/SOURCE_MANIFEST.json and delivery.json, which identify these bytes.",
